# This repository exists to reproduce one specific, hardware-verified recovery
# build, so git should store and check out file contents verbatim rather than
# rewriting line endings on the way in or out.
#
# The case that matters is *.patch. Two of the OrangeFox theme files
# (gui/theme/portrait_hdpi/themes/style.xml and themes/styles/Cream.xml) are
# CRLF throughout, so any patch touching them carries CRLF context lines. With
# core.autocrlf=input those get normalised to LF on commit.
#
# git apply tolerates that mismatch, but GNU patch -p1 does not, and the stored
# patch would no longer be a faithful record of what was verified on the device.
* -text
